1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:10,200
Voice apps speak different languages. Your browser uses WebRTC. Your
phone system uses SIP. And your AI assistant needs to reach a human.

2
00:00:10,520 --> 00:00:21,570
Bridgefu connects those worlds. It's a Rust media gateway built on
rvoip. Two call legs. One bridge for bidirectional audio, keypad
tones, and explicitly allowed context.

3
00:00:21,890 --> 00:00:28,840
Bridgefu handles protocol boundaries and converts codecs when needed,
so each side can keep its own stack.

4
00:00:29,160 --> 00:00:37,310
One reference workflow connects a Vapi SIP transfer to Amazon Connect,
carrying a correlation ID for an agent screen pop.

5
00:00:37,630 --> 00:00:45,230
Define a route, choose a declarative recipe, and try an encrypted SIP
to WebRTC call locally.

6
00:00:45,550 --> 00:00:50,000
Bridgefu. Connect anything. Start with the local demos on GitHub.
